        "Processing": {
          "Process_Category": "Laser-based powder bed fusion (PBF-LB)",
          "Process_Text": {
            "original": "The gas-atomization powder was fabricated by LangFeng Material Technology Co., Ltd. The PBF-LB process was conducted using an EOS M100 Laser-sintering system equipped with a 200 W fiber laser and a laser spot diameter of 40 μm. The adopted optimized parameters were a laser power (P) of 100 W, a scan speed (v) of 1000 mm/s, a hatch spacing (h) of 0.05 mm, and a layer thickness (t) of 0.02 mm. Prior to the AM process, a 20 μm thick layer of powder was deposited onto a 304 stainless-steel build platform without preheating in a high-purity argon environment (<1000 ppm oxygen). After each scan, a new layer of powder was deposited, and the laser scanning direction was rotated by 67° relative to the previous layer.",
            "simplified": "Gas-atomized AlCoCrFeNi2.1 powder (15–53 μm, avg 31.5 μm) processed by PBF-LB (EOS M100) with 100 W laser power, 1000 mm/s scan speed, 0.05 mm hatch spacing, 0.02 mm layer thickness, 40 μm spot size, no preheating, Ar atmosphere, 67° rotation between layers. As-built plates: 40 mm × 8 mm × 4 mm, relative density >99%."
