        "Structure": {
          "Structure_Text": {
            "original": "A dual-phase hierarchical microstructure is achieved in the as-built AlCoCrFeNi2.1 EHEA. The as-built EHEA exhibits a lower volume fraction of the FCC phase (16.4%) and a much higher volume fraction of the B2 phase (83.6%). The lamellar colonies are composed of alternating FCC and ordered B2 nanolayers. The as-built microstructure has no precipitates in the FCC and B2 matrix. A high density of dislocations is present due to the rapid solidification of PBF-LB. Cellular colonies are primarily composed of the BCC phase with a high density of dislocations, adopting an ordered-B2 structure encapsulated by a disordered FCC interfacial nanolayer.",
            "simplified": "Dual-phase hierarchical microstructure: B2-dominated (83.6 vol%) with minor FCC (16.4 vol%). Two types of eutectic colonies: nano-lamellar (alternating FCC/B2 layers) and cellular (B2 core + FCC shell). No precipitates. High dislocation density. Bicontinuous Ni-Al-rich and Co-Cr-Fe-rich nanostructures within B2 colonies suggest spinodal decomposition."
          },
